+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Voyage 1
+
+**Goal:** Implement TodoMVC per `assets/app-spec.md` and `assets/app-template.index.html`. Vanilla JS, no preprocessors, localStorage persistence.
+
+**Specs authored:**
+- `features/todos.feature` - 15 scenarios: add, toggle all, counter, clear completed, section visibility, focus
+- `features/todo-item.feature` - 9 scenarios: toggle, edit, destroy, double-click
+- `features/routing.feature` - 8 scenarios: filter views, hash routing, filter highlighting, live filter updates
+- `features/persistence.feature` - 3 scenarios: localStorage persistence across reload
+
+**Watchbill:** `watchbill.json` with 4 watches ordered: core list operations, item interactions, routing, persistence.
+
+**Tier:** All scenarios in `@logic` default tier. No sandbox or external service needed.
+
+**Key decisions:**
+- Specs use `happy-dom` via `@cucumber/cucumber` for browser DOM simulation in step definitions (no real browser needed for Voyage 1)
+- localStorage key: `todos-todomvc` per the spec's `todos-[framework]` pattern
+- Routing uses hash-based `#/active`, `#/completed` per the spec
+
+**Deck status:** Clean. Specs written, watchbill written. No commit made.
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e8e5dd2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+Feature: Persistence to localStorage
+  As a user who returns to the app
+  I want my todos preserved across page loads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist across page reload
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the todo "Walk dog" appears in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    And the todo "Walk dog" is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Completed state persists across page reload
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    And the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Removed todos do not reappear on reload
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the user clicks the destroy button for "Buy milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is removed
+    And the todo "Walk dog" appears in the list
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ce9f092
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+Feature: Routing and filtering
+  As a user viewing filtered todos
+  I want to filter by All, Active, or Completed
+  So that I see only the relevant todos
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is visible
+    And the todo "Walk dog" is visible
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is hidden
+    And the todo "Walk dog" is visible
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is visible
+    And the todo "Walk dog" is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is highlighted
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the "Active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter is highlighted
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the "Completed" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: All filter is highlighted by default
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the "All" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo in Active view hides it
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk" on
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Uncompleting a todo in Completed view hides it
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk" off
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is hidden
diff --git a/features/todo-item.feature b/features/todo-item.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7b513fb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-item.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+Feature: Todo item interactions
+  As a user interacting with a todo
+  I want to toggle, edit, and remove individual todos
+  So that I manage each task precisely
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+
+  Scenario: Clicking checkbox marks todo as completed
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy milk" on
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+
+  Scenario: Clicking completed checkbox unmarks todo
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy milk" off
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking label activates edit mode
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is in edit mode
+    And the edit input contains "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Edit saves on Enter
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in edit mode
+    When the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy oat milk" appears in the list
+    And the todo "Buy oat milk" is not in edit mode
+
+  Scenario: Edit saves on blur
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in edit mode
+    When the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input and blurs
+    Then the todo "Buy oat milk" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Edit discards on Escape
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in edit mode
+    When the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input and presses Escape
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is not in edit mode
+
+  Scenario: Edit trims whitespace
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in edit mode
+    When the user types "  Buy oat milk  " in the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy oat milk" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit destroys the todo
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in edit mode
+    When the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is removed
+
+  Scenario: Clicking destroy button removes the todo
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the destroy button for "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is removed
diff --git a/features/todos.feature b/features/todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c3d0496
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+Feature: Todo list management
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to add, toggle, edit, and remove todos
+  So that I track what needs to be done
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no existing todos
+
+  Scenario: New todo is created on Enter
+    Given the new todo input is focused
+    When the user types "Buy milk" and presses Enter
+    Then a todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the new todo input is empty
+    And the todo is not completed
+
+  Scenario: New todo trims whitespace
+    When the user types "  Buy milk  " and presses Enter
+    Then a todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Empty or whitespace input is not created
+    When the user types "   " and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: New todo input clears after creation
+    When the user types "Buy milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the new todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: Main section and footer are hidden when no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Main section and footer appear when a todo exists
+    When the user types "Buy milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the main section is visible
+    And the footer is visible
+
+  Scenario: Todo input is focused on page load
+    Then the new todo input has focus
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all sets all todos to completed
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos are completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all clears when a todo is unchecked
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And all todos are completed
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy milk" off
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all checks when all todos are completed individually
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    When the user completes all todos individually
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows correct active count
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    Then the counter shows "2 items left"
+    When the user completes the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter uses singular for one active item
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button removes completed todos
+    Given the user has added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the user clicks "Clear completed"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is removed
+    And the todo "Walk dog" remains
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button hidden when no completed todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button visible when completed todos exist
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is visible
